course: dictionary
lesson: 1363
title: A tube in the hospital
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A cannula is a thin tube that doctors and nurses put into the body. Context helps you work out what it is. «An anaesthetist gives the anaesthetic by mask or through a cannula, a thin plastic tube in a vein.» The words after the comma explain the word: it is a thin plastic tube, and it goes in a vein.
explain: Ask yourself what would fit in the sentence. A needle goes in the skin, but a tube stays in the vein. «Numbing cream put on about an hour before makes the skin numb so a needle or cannula hurts less.» Here the cannula sits next to a needle, so it is something that goes into the body, like a needle does.
explain: Try your meaning in the sentence. Put in "a thin tube put into a vein" and read it again. If it still makes sense, your meaning is probably right. If not, read the words around it again and look for more clues.
fact: A cannula is a thin tube put into a vein or into the body.
fact: Doctors and nurses use it so medicine or fluid can go in, or fluid can come out.
fact: A needle puts the cannula in. Then the needle comes out, and the soft plastic tube stays.
fact: A nasal cannula is a small tube under the nose that gives oxygen.
fact: The plural of cannula can be cannulas or cannulae.
exercise: «An anaesthetist gives the anaesthetic through a cannula, a thin plastic tube in a vein.» What is a cannula? | A hospital bed | A long wooden stick | *A thin plastic tube put into a vein | A kind of sweet medicine
exercise: «Numbing cream makes the skin numb so a needle or cannula hurts less.» What does numb mean here? | Full of blood | *Not able to feel pain | Loud and noisy | Very hot and sore
exercise: A nurse says, «The cannula is in the back of my hand.» Where is the cannula? | Under the bed | *In the back of the hand | On the head | In the mouth
test: «A nasal cannula is a small tube under the nose that gives oxygen.» What does a nasal cannula give? | Medicine in a glass | Water | *Oxygen | Sugar
test: Why does a doctor use a cannula in a vein? | To cut the patient's hair | To make the patient taller | *So medicine or fluid can go in | To keep the room warm
exam: «The needle comes out, but the soft plastic tube stays in the vein.» What stays in the vein? | *The cannula | The needle | The anaesthetic | The hospital bed
